// check: accepted
// CROWN modal (§11 6.3's crucible sweep): the LATENT/PERFORMED
// distinction — mk constructs and RETURNS the closure without calling
// it, so mk's own row is pure and E rides the returned VALUE's row
// (the crown's flow-edge law). The !E on mk accepts; the escape's
// refusal lives at the CALL site (leak-escape-negation's shape).
// Expect NO E_EffectMismatch.
effect E { op() -> Int }
fn mk() with !E = () => op()
fn main() = 0
